34,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems our delays are quite predictable. Projects based on ""appeal"" often slip, and the weather takes a heavy toll on our outdoor work.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Oh! I found out that some of our fancy specialist rooms are barely used, while the general rooms are totally packed! We should focus on that!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The data is concerning. Our technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks that should be automated, and the staffing gap is only widening.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I've noticed a pattern. The projects that failed to satisfy users were those that were too restrictive. Also, the older blocks are a minefield of hidden costs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"How fascinating. It appears our ""approved"" costs are mere suggestions. The market has moved on, yet our budget sheets are stuck in the past.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, that explains so much. If we keep underestimating, we keep rushing the end of the project to fit the fiscal year.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, you saw the reviews too! It's so clear that we need to make spaces that everyone can use, not just a few people!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shizue, the rushing you mention is exactly what burns out the staff. They are the ones who fix the mistakes made in haste.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I sympathize. If we choose a plan for an older block, we must account for the hazardous materials I found in the surveys.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. And we must consider that we have no reserve for the equipment we're replacing. We are essentially spending money we don't have.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I feel for the staff. Perhaps we should choose a project that is straightforward and doesn't rely on ""appeal"" or outdoor work.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,But we can't just be safe! We have to make sure the students have rooms to study in! The general room shortage is a real problem!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"Safety and stability are not ""just being safe,"" Yumi. They are the foundation. We need a plan that reduces the manual burden on our staff.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,Let's look for a middle ground. A project that increases general accessibility but avoids the high-risk zones of the older blocks.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A logical approach. Though I suspect any ""middle ground"" will still be underestimated by twenty percent if we follow the current trend.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
